    'c51c1e5f-5cc1-4b77-8832-2d10cc97f22d',
    'model_cbf_lvo_aortic_dissection_acute',
    'Cerebral malperfusion from aortic dissection — acute state (Cases 33 aortic dissection, 34). Dissection involving aortic arch extends into carotid origins, producing dynamic or fixed cerebral malperfusion — variable CBF reduction depending on extent of false lumen compression of carotid ostia. Modelled as significant but not complete R_As_CaBV elevation (partial flow still possible via contralateral carotid or vertebral). Severely elevated systemic BP (type A dissection typically presents with hypertension before cardiac tamponade). Thrombolysis absolutely contraindicated.',
