    'c51c1e5f-5cc1-4b77-8832-2d10cc97f237',
    'model_cbf_post_thrombectomy_sickle_cell_exchange_2d',
    'Post exchange transfusion and mechanical thrombectomy for sickle cell LVO — 2-3 day state (Case 40). Exchange transfusion reduces HbS fraction and improves rheology: reflected in slightly normalised C_CaBV (less vessel stiffening as sickling reduced), improved oxygen-carrying capacity (volume targets restored toward normal). Thrombectomy achieves recanalization. Cerebrovascular vasculopathy from sickle cell is irreversible: C_CaBV remains below healthy baseline. Mild reperfusion oedema expected (C_SAS moderately reduced). Ongoing sickle cell vasculopathy risk persists long-term.',
